# Your server's settings, all in one place (#440). setup.sh writes this file
# for you; by hand, copy it to `.env` next to compose.yaml, run
# `chmod 600 .env` so only you can read it (#506), and fill in LINGER_DOMAIN.
# compose.yaml and the Caddyfile read everything from here, so you never edit
# them. It's also where the relay's secret lives: keep it out of anything you
# share.

# Your server's name, without https://, such as linger.example.com. Point it,
# and the same name with cdn. in front, at this machine (host guide, step 2).
# Voice goes to the address it points at.
LINGER_DOMAIN=

# --- The voice relay (optional, for networks that block voice) ---------------
# Its shared secret: Linger signs short-lived relay passwords with it and
# coturn checks them with it. Make one with `openssl rand -hex 32`, then take
# the # off COMPOSE_PROFILES so the relay starts with everything else. The
# relay carries voice to the address below (or the one LINGER_DOMAIN points
# at) and nowhere else.
LINGER_TURN_SECRET=
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=voice
# Behind a home router, or a cloud network, rather than holding its public
# address itself? The relay has to be told that address. setup.sh fills this
# in when it sees something in front of the machine.
# LINGER_RELAY_EXTERNAL_IP=203.0.113.7

# --- Settings you might want: take the # off to use one -----------------------

# How much this server holds in total (default 50GB). On a 50 GB disk, 10GB
# leaves room for the system and Docker.
# LINGER_POOL_BYTES=10GB

# When old files are deleted. when-full (the default) keeps them until the
# server needs the room: past 90% of LINGER_POOL_BYTES the oldest go first,
# until it's under 80%. A number of days deletes each file that long after it
# was shared, however much room there is; off keeps them all. A starred file,
# and a file on a pinned message, never go.
# LINGER_FILE_EXPIRY_DAYS=when-full

# The server copies its database into data/backups every night, keeping a
# week of nightly copies and a month of weekly ones. off stops it, if you back
# the data folder up another way. They're on this disk, so keep a copy
# somewhere else too (host guide, Backups).
# LINGER_BACKUPS=off

# Where voice goes: an IP address to use instead of the one LINGER_DOMAIN
# points at (a domain behind Cloudflare's proxy needs this), or off for a
# server with no voice. The server and the relay both read it.
# LINGER_VOICE_ADDRESS=203.0.113.7

# How many people may sign up from one network in an hour (default 60, all at
# once if need be, then the rest spread over the hour), or off for no limit.
# Raise it when a big group is joining together from one place: a school, an
# office, or a phone network that puts many people behind one address. The
# invite still decides who can join.
# LINGER_SIGNUPS_PER_HOUR=500

# How many passwords the server checks at the same time (default 4, up to
# 256). Each check holds about 19 MB of memory and a CPU core for a moment, so
# N at once can take N x 19 MB: 4 is 76 MB, 16 is about 300 MB. Raise it if
# people are told the server is busy and the machine has the cores and memory;
# more than the number of cores makes nobody faster.
# LINGER_PASSWORD_CHECKS_AT_ONCE=8

# Proxies Linger believes about who's connecting, for its limits on signing
# in and signing up (default: private, meaning this machine and private
# networks, which is how Caddy here connects). Only for a proxy somewhere
# else, such as Caddy on another machine reaching this one over Tailscale.
# Addresses and ranges, separated by commas; keep private to keep the default.
# LINGER_TRUSTED_PROXIES=private,100.64.0.0/10

# Files served from a name other than cdn.<LINGER_DOMAIN>. It has to differ
# from LINGER_DOMAIN, and the Caddyfile's second name has to match it.
# LINGER_MEDIA_DOMAIN=files.linger.example.com

# Files in an S3 bucket instead of ./data/objects. Cloudflare R2 is the one to
# pick, because it charges nothing for bytes going out. The server refuses to
# start if any of these are missing.
# LINGER_STORAGE=s3
# LINGER_S3_BUCKET=linger
# LINGER_S3_ENDPOINT=https://ACCOUNT.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# LINGER_S3_REGION=auto
# LINGER_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# LINGER_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...

# Send each night's copy of the database to a bucket too, so it survives this
# machine (host guide, Backups). Its own settings, so files can stay on this
# disk; it can be the same bucket as the files, and the copies go under
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_PREFIX (default backups/). Off unless the bucket and both
# keys are set, and the server refuses to start with only some of them.
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=linger-backups
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://ACCOUNT.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_REGION=auto
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# LINGER_BACKUP_S3_PREFIX=backups/
